From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 38/43] Metal diamond engine: seven tilings in a two-stage
 tuner; per-tile lists in a buffer of their own (snapshot cg30l)

A sweep of thirteen tilings on eight models added three candidates: K=4 with tiles 10,6 (6-8 % ahead of the four on
a 3 M cell box and on patch x5), K=4 with tiles 9,2 (the shape of luikore's engine, 10 % ahead on a 17 M cell box of
257 z lines) and K=5 with tiles 12,8 (5 % on notch x3). OPENEMS_DIAMOND_CAND=n keeps the first n. So that more
candidates do not mean more steps of tuning, a tiling that is more than 6 % behind the fastest after two timed
command buffers is not timed further. The per-tile lists of a tiling are in a buffer of their own, so the shared
extension words (the UPML indices among them) are no longer copied once per tiling. Against snapshot cg29, paired
rounds on a loaded machine: GCPW line x1.09, SMA launch x1.15, a 3 M cell box x1.20, a 17 M cell box x1.16, notch x3
x1.14, patch x5 x1.06. diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical; check --lite on six models, debye-check, validate on the
Metal engine (15 of 15) and the GCPW end-to-end run on the Metal engine pass.

